      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would recommend a logic system that loads in lower file sizes first then once most are done the client would start to load in the larger file sizes. This could just be an optimizing feature instead of as said before a possible blanket ban of big avatars. Some people hang out with animators and their avatars tend to be relatively big. I wouldn’t want to force people to go down the list one by one after to just unhindered the avatars assuming that option would be allowed.",
